- [ ] **Fragments (15 files)**: All fragment_*.xml files
- [ ] **Items (12 files)**: All item_*.xml files  
- [ ] **Dialogs (6 files)**: All dialog_*.xml files
- [ ] **Bottom Sheets (4 files)**: All bottom_sheet_*.xml files
- [ ] **Views (8 files)**: All view_*.xml files
- [ ] **Layouts (5 files)**: layout_*.xml files

### **🎯 Implementation Strategy**:
1. **Batch Convert Colors**: Use regex find/replace for common patterns
2. **Test Each File**: Ensure no visual regressions
3. **Validate Themes**: Test with all 8 festival themes
4. **Performance Check**: Monitor build times and app performance

## 📝 **Phase 4: Advanced Features**

### **🌟 Dynamic Theme Features**:
- [ ] **Real-time Preview**: Live theme switching in settings
- [ ] **Template-based Themes**: Auto-theme based on template colors
- [ ] **Accessibility Themes**: High contrast and large text variants
- [ ] **Seasonal Auto-switching**: Automatic theme changes based on calendar

### **🚀 Performance Optimizations**:
- [ ] **Theme Caching**: Cache theme resources for faster switching
- [ ] **Lazy Loading**: Load theme variants only when needed
- [ ] **Memory Management**: Optimize theme resource usage

## 📊 **Success Metrics**:
- **100% Theme Attribute Usage**: No hardcoded colors in layouts
- **Smooth Theme Switching**: < 500ms theme change time
- **Visual Consistency**: All components follow Material 3 guidelines
- **Accessibility Compliance**: WCAG AA standards met
- **Performance**: No impact on app startup or navigation speed

## 🔄 **Testing Strategy**:
1. **Theme Switching Tests**: Verify all 8 themes work correctly
2. **Device Compatibility**: Test on different screen sizes and Android versions
3. **Accessibility Testing**: Screen readers, high contrast, large text
4. **Performance Benchmarks**: Memory usage, startup time, theme switch speed
5. **Visual Regression**: Screenshot comparison across themes

## 📈 **Implementation Timeline**:
- **Week 1**: Phase 1 - Core layout centralization
- **Week 2**: Phase 2 - UI enhancements (chips, navigation, full screen)
- **Week 3**: Phase 3 - Complete layout folder analysis and updates
- **Week 4**: Phase 4 - Advanced features and optimization
- **Week 5**: Testing, refinement, and documentation